// The polynomial ACCELERATED TACTIC (--fast path). This theory declares add/mul but proves
// NONE of the ring lemmas — so `polynomial` cannot build a certificate here
// (under the default it hard-errors "needs mulAddDistribLeft in scope").
//
// Under --fast, the accelerated tactic decides the identity by comparing bare syntactic
// semiring normal forms — trusting that add/mul ARE a commutative semiring,
// which this theory never proves. That presumption about uninterpreted symbols
// is exactly why the result is ACCELERATED (accelerated: polynomial). Run with
// --fast; the golden shows the acceleration + the ACCELERATED banner.
sort Nat
const ZERO: Nat
const ONE: Nat
func add(a: Nat, b: Nat): Nat
func mul(a: Nat, b: Nat): Nat

// distribute + reorder + fold — all decided structurally by the accelerated tactic.
theorem ringIdentity: forall a, b, c: Nat;
  mul(add(a, b), c) = add(mul(c, b), mul(c, a))
proof
  @conclusion |
    forall a, b, c: Nat; mul(add(a, b), c) = add(mul(c, b), mul(c, a))
    [using polynomial_quantified]
qed
